1
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:24,240
Anyone without money, come to my place!

2
00:00:24,240 --> 00:00:28,960
I've got none either, but don't worry.

3
00:00:28,960 --> 00:00:36,020
Look, blue sky and white clouds!

4
00:00:36,020 --> 00:00:36,420
Me

5
00:00:39,020 --> 00:00:42,900
We'll manage somehow, right?

6
00:00:55,900 --> 00:00:59,860
Anyone without a job, come to my place!

7
00:00:59,860 --> 00:01:04,480
I've got none either, but don't worry.

8
00:01:04,480 --> 00:01:11,900
Look, even the burning sun, too!

9
00:01:13,420 --> 00:01:18,240
Somehow or other, it'll all work out.

10
00:01:20,300 --> 00:01:23,480
You understand, right? Got it, got it.

11
00:01:23,480 --> 00:01:27,400
Once you understand, shut up and follow me!

12
00:01:41,820 --> 00:01:44,220
Why not drink sake?

13
00:01:44,220 --> 00:01:46,700
Why not get drunk?

14
00:01:51,040 --> 00:01:53,100
Hello, ancestors!

15
00:01:57,100 --> 00:01:57,540
What?

16
00:01:57,860 --> 00:01:58,040
What?

17
00:01:58,300 --> 00:02:00,480
That old man who got arrested
for drinking without paying,

18
00:02:00,480 --> 00:02:02,340
claiming to rule over Asakusa?

19
00:02:02,980 --> 00:02:04,160
Don't know, don't know.

20
00:02:04,480 --> 00:02:05,740
We don't have any old man like that here.

21
00:02:06,680 --> 00:02:07,700
Wait, could it be...

22
00:02:08,160 --> 00:02:10,260
Fine, I'll go check it out anyway.

23
00:02:11,440 --> 00:02:12,160
Mom

24
00:02:12,160 --> 00:02:14,160
Old Kanbei from Tsukudajima

25
00:02:14,160 --> 00:02:15,460
do you know where he went?

26
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:18,120
apparently he's gone on
a trip to the Maldives.

27
00:02:18,600 --> 00:02:19,480
The Maldives?

28
00:02:19,480 --> 00:02:20,620
That's probably fake, right?

29
00:02:21,020 --> 00:02:23,040
So that means the one who
ate and drank without paying

30
00:02:23,040 --> 00:02:24,820
has nothing to do with me, that domain

31
00:02:25,200 --> 00:02:27,700
He'll probably be back by Obon, right?

32
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:29,120
Well, I'm busy.

33
00:02:29,120 --> 00:02:30,500
Okay, I'm hanging up, Mom.

34
00:02:30,500 --> 00:02:32,640
If you don't respect your ancestors,

35
00:02:32,640 --> 00:02:33,560
you'll be punished.

36
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:38,440
Got it.
Did you find out who that old man is?

37
00:02:38,980 --> 00:02:44,380
He's saying such nonsense, insisting
that he was born in the 6th year of Kaei.

38
00:02:44,380 --> 00:02:49,760
Kaei? What's that supposed to be? The 6th year of Kaei is from the Edo period,
I think.

39
00:02:50,220 --> 00:02:55,440
But that would make him 160 years old this year.
Nah, no way.

40
00:02:55,440 --> 00:03:00,360
The old man introduced himself as Tameyoshi Ryotsu,
so it's probably...

41
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:08,160
Do you have any idea? Tameyoshi... I've heard that name somewhere.
He's not your relative, is he? No, no, I don't know him.

42
00:03:08,160 --> 00:03:12,700
Anyway, until we find that old man, please
keep cooperating with us a little longer.

43
00:03:14,940 --> 00:03:18,460
Well then, senpai,
I'll head back to the police box first.

44
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:27,200
Why do I, someone with no connection to this,
have to find the old man who skipped out on his bill?

45
00:03:27,200 --> 00:03:29,020
You're not unconnected to this.

46
00:03:29,440 --> 00:03:30,420
It's me.

47
00:03:30,420 --> 00:03:31,600
Great-grandson.

48
00:03:32,060 --> 00:03:36,060
Ryotsu Tameyoshi is your great-grandfather,
and that's the end of it.

49
00:03:36,480 --> 00:03:39,460
Great-grandfather? He's been gone for ages.

50
00:03:39,460 --> 00:03:42,420
Tameyoshi has been causing problems
for as long as anyone can remember.

51
00:03:42,420 --> 00:03:47,160
He was already a person of concern,
but escaping from heaven is unprecedented.

52
00:03:48,460 --> 00:03:48,932
Listen,

53
00:03:48,982 --> 00:03:52,900
as his great-grandson, you're responsible.
Find Tameyoshi right away!

54
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:55,680
Me? Finding him is your job!

55
00:03:57,860 --> 00:04:01,440
Look at this! Two more demerit points
and you're going straight to hell!

56
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:05,140
If you go to hell, you'll be stuck there forever,
in eternal needle hell!

57
00:04:05,740 --> 00:04:06,380
Hell?

58
00:04:07,580 --> 00:04:10,918
But if you find Tameyoshi and hand him over,

59
00:04:10,968 --> 00:04:15,280
I'll wipe out all of your penalty points.
That's the deal!

60
00:04:18,460 --> 00:04:23,280
What is this? Where am I? Ginza?

61
00:04:24,640 --> 00:04:32,080
Is this really Ginza? I've only been gone a little while, and it's like the West now.
Everyone's gone and put on Western clothes.

62
00:04:33,400 --> 00:04:40,620
I see, so I've come back to life. It must be a
reward for my good conduct. Now it all makes sense.

63
00:04:40,620 --> 00:04:41,960
Whoa, hold on!

64
00:04:41,960 --> 00:04:43,440
Don't suddenly jump out like that!

65
00:04:43,440 --> 00:04:44,180
I want to die.

66
00:04:44,180 --> 00:04:49,040
So, an ancient fossil of an old man
who lived through the late Edo period

67
00:04:49,040 --> 00:04:50,980
is wandering around somewhere, is that it?

68
00:04:50,980 --> 00:04:53,080
But you're a wizard, aren't you?

69
00:04:53,080 --> 00:04:55,200
Can you catch him quickly?

70
00:04:56,020 --> 00:04:58,400
Searching for something
that isn't of this world

71
00:04:58,400 --> 00:05:01,960
is a far more backbreaking job
than searching for a living person.

72
00:05:02,600 --> 00:05:06,080
On top of that, if we don't bring him back soon,
my country will be in danger too.

73
00:05:07,260 --> 00:05:09,520
I can't let those words slide.

74
00:05:10,840 --> 00:05:11,541
So, in other words,

75
00:05:11,591 --> 00:05:15,160
The reason Tameyoshi-jiisan
escaped from heaven is,

76
00:05:15,210 --> 00:05:18,060
So that makes it your responsibility,
is that it?

77
00:05:18,900 --> 00:05:22,194
If we don't bring the old man
back before the boss finds out,

78
00:05:22,244 --> 00:05:24,424
when your supervisory
failure comes to light,

79
00:05:24,474 --> 00:05:27,540
your neck is on the line, is that right?

80
00:05:27,780 --> 00:05:28,900
Ahahaha!

81
00:05:29,180 --> 00:05:30,160
Nope, forget it!

82
00:05:30,340 --> 00:05:32,320
What's going on?

83
00:05:32,540 --> 00:05:36,060
I've quit looking for that old man.
I've called it off.

84
00:05:36,540 --> 00:05:39,400
Hey? Wait, wait, wait.

85
00:05:40,620 --> 00:05:49,060
Not just wipe my disciplinary record, give me a reward too.
Then I'll find Tameyoshi-jiisan. Taking advantage of my weakness

86
00:05:50,300 --> 00:06:00,520
If you don't want to... what do you want? Wipe out all my past penalty points,
and on top of that, no penalty points for the next hundred years.

87
00:06:01,420 --> 00:06:05,120
There's no way I can do
something like that on my own.

88
00:06:05,800 --> 00:06:06,960
You heartless creep!

89
00:06:07,340 --> 00:06:07,660
Then,

90
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:08,400
Fine, fine.

91
00:06:09,720 --> 00:06:11,480
Then it's a deal.

92
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:12,040
Yeah.

93
00:06:12,820 --> 00:06:15,200
Come to think of it,
the cars haven't moved at all.

94
00:06:16,780 --> 00:06:20,121
Yes. I swerved to avoid an
old man who suddenly darted out,

95
00:06:20,171 --> 00:06:23,020
and when I slammed on the brakes,
the car behind rear-ended me.

96
00:06:23,700 --> 00:06:25,711
I was also trying to avoid that old man,

97
00:06:25,761 --> 00:06:29,240
so I hit the brakes in a panic, and of
course the car behind crashed into me.

98
00:06:30,620 --> 00:06:33,000
Hey, what was that old man wearing?

99
00:06:33,220 --> 00:06:35,100
Also, a kimono...

100
00:06:35,100 --> 00:06:36,080
He was dressed in momohiki.

101
00:06:36,080 --> 00:06:37,000
Well?

102
00:06:37,100 --> 00:06:38,040
No doubt about it.

103
00:06:38,900 --> 00:06:41,740
If we don't catch him soon,
we're in for big trouble.

104
00:06:42,740 --> 00:06:44,200
It really suits you, ma'am.

105
00:06:44,620 --> 00:06:46,420
This one's nice too, but...

106
00:06:46,420 --> 00:06:46,802
And also,

107
00:06:46,852 --> 00:06:50,460
this is our tennis coach,
who joined us just yesterday.

108
00:06:53,240 --> 00:06:54,862
Excuse me, sir, but

109
00:06:54,912 --> 00:06:57,420
please don't press up against the window.

110
00:06:58,020 --> 00:07:00,880
A greengrocer who ate udon, please.

111
00:07:02,520 --> 00:07:03,640
Please stop.

112
00:07:03,640 --> 00:07:07,480
Fine, fine. What a powerful woman you are.

113
00:07:07,480 --> 00:07:11,980
The greengrocer and the udon shop are
both just past the next traffic light,

114
00:07:11,980 --> 00:07:13,020
so please head that way.

115
00:07:13,420 --> 00:07:14,260
What about the liquor store?

116
00:07:14,420 --> 00:07:15,440
There's one, probably.

117
00:07:15,440 --> 00:07:17,080
I see. Right, this way.

118
00:07:17,080 --> 00:07:18,640
What is it?

119
00:07:20,160 --> 00:07:23,660
My apologies. As for other new releases this season,
they're over here.

120
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:38,900
He's not here either. Searching house by house won't get us anywhere. Let's split up and look.
As for your magic staff, I was in such a hurry when I rushed out that I left it at the Heaven Police's... sixth...

121
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:43,440
I forgot it. Then you can't use magic. You're just a useless old geezer,
aren't you?

122
00:07:43,900 --> 00:07:50,300
Sorry for being just a useless old geezer. I'll go get the staff,
so catch Tameyoshi if you find him in the meantime.

123
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:53,106
You're running back? But,

124
00:07:53,156 --> 00:07:57,440
isn't there a better
way to find the old man?

125
00:07:57,820 --> 00:08:00,220
Right, booze.

126
00:08:02,940 --> 00:08:05,080
Hello. It's already this late tonight.

127
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:07,340
Thank you so much for your kindness.

128
00:08:07,400 --> 00:08:10,098
Today, since it's a hospitality
dish that's easy to make,

129
00:08:10,148 --> 00:08:12,300
I'd like to try making chirashi-zushi.

130
00:08:13,480 --> 00:08:14,600
Yes, understood.

131
00:08:15,340 --> 00:08:18,900
Sounds great, chirashi-zushi.
You all love it too, right?

132
00:08:20,300 --> 00:08:20,800
I love it.

133
00:08:20,800 --> 00:08:23,320
Then frozen ones are fine,

134
00:08:23,320 --> 00:08:24,760
so please prepare some eel.

135
00:08:25,140 --> 00:08:26,240
Eel?

136
00:08:26,480 --> 00:08:27,500
E-eel.

137
00:08:28,820 --> 00:08:30,440
Sorry, I right now

138
00:08:30,440 --> 00:08:32,060
don't have any cash on me.

139
00:08:32,060 --> 00:08:32,960
Old man,

140
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:35,140
that's a TV, you know.

141
00:08:35,140 --> 00:08:38,040
I finally feel like I've met someone I know.

142
00:08:38,040 --> 00:08:39,880
Which crew are you from?

143
00:08:39,880 --> 00:08:40,860
Well

144
00:08:41,300 --> 00:08:43,780
we're filming right nearby,

145
00:08:43,780 --> 00:08:45,340
as extras for a Bakumatsu war drama.

146
00:08:45,340 --> 00:08:46,800
Please, help yourself if you like.

147
00:08:47,480 --> 00:08:48,300
T-Tora...

148
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:54,000
Here you can see all kinds of
materials from the late Edo period.

149
00:08:54,000 --> 00:08:56,520
You look pretty good in that.

150
00:08:56,520 --> 00:08:57,800
What's that?

151
00:08:58,580 --> 00:08:59,560
Ryoma-san.

152
00:09:00,520 --> 00:09:02,320
I'll return the dolly later, okay?

153
00:09:02,320 --> 00:09:07,160
With this much, we can draw that old man in.

154
00:09:07,600 --> 00:09:10,520
It's me, Tameyoshi of Sukudania.

155
00:09:12,380 --> 00:09:14,140
Have you forgotten me?

156
00:09:15,780 --> 00:09:20,020
It's Tameyoshi, who always tagged along after you back then,
right up to your death.

157
00:09:20,300 --> 00:09:22,120
Look closely, come on.

158
00:09:22,120 --> 00:09:25,300
Hey, Ryoma-san, say something!

159
00:09:26,020 --> 00:09:27,280
Well then, Sensei, I'm in your hands.

160
00:09:27,280 --> 00:09:27,920
Yes.

161
00:09:29,160 --> 00:09:32,840
Now, Professor Oyamada, who is also the organizer
and supervisor of this Bakumatsu exhibition,

162
00:09:32,840 --> 00:09:35,820
we would like to ask him a few questions.

163
00:09:36,460 --> 00:09:37,680
Oyamada speaking.

164
00:09:38,500 --> 00:09:40,040
I've turned into such an old geezer.

165
00:09:40,040 --> 00:09:42,700
Back then, I was just a 12-
or 13-year-old kid.

166
00:09:42,700 --> 00:09:45,040
It's no wonder you don't recognize me.

167
00:09:46,640 --> 00:09:49,240
You've gotten quite quiet, Ryoma.

168
00:09:50,300 --> 00:09:53,680
Grandpa, though it looks just like the real thing,
this is a wax figure.

169
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:55,540
A wax figure?

170
00:09:56,540 --> 00:09:58,860
Wow, this is a wax figure?

171
00:09:59,540 --> 00:10:02,360
Let's interview some
of the visitors as well.

172
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:05,860
Sir, are you also a fan of Ryoma Sakamoto?

173
00:10:06,300 --> 00:10:08,980
Yes, I'm Ryotsu Tameyoshi.

174
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:12,020
So you're a fan of Ryoma Sakamoto.

175
00:10:12,680 --> 00:10:17,357
Back in the day, I often delivered tsukudani,
Ryoma's favorite, to the restaurant.

176
00:10:17,407 --> 00:10:18,420
That's right.

177
00:10:20,300 --> 00:10:21,272
The lion of the Bakumatsu,

178
00:10:21,322 --> 00:10:24,680
even today, still leaves a deep impression
on the hearts of the Japanese people.

179
00:10:24,820 --> 00:10:26,500
So that was after delivering it, right?

180
00:10:26,680 --> 00:10:29,400
No, I remember this photo very well.

181
00:10:29,540 --> 00:10:31,580
I'm pretty sure I was around here.

182
00:10:32,060 --> 00:10:33,540
Are you a fan of the Bakumatsu period?

183
00:10:34,120 --> 00:10:37,440
It's the era I lived in.
Not that I have any like or dislike for it.

184
00:10:37,520 --> 00:10:41,340
I remember this one too.
Back then I was watching from around here.

185
00:10:42,580 --> 00:10:46,360
Photos are fine. The flash goes off like
lightning and it's a bit scary, though.

186
00:10:46,460 --> 00:10:49,300
We should have had lots of
photos of Ryoma-san at home, too.

187
00:10:50,320 --> 00:10:51,420
Is that really true?

188
00:10:52,260 --> 00:10:55,500
I even went to see Saigo
Takamori when he came to Edo.

189
00:10:55,500 --> 00:10:58,380
It's hard to believe all at once, but

190
00:10:58,380 --> 00:11:00,580
Maybe it's worth checking.

191
00:11:01,080 --> 00:11:01,860
Back in those days,

192
00:11:04,480 --> 00:11:06,480
this smells like sake.

193
00:11:10,200 --> 00:11:12,940
Normally we'd be lighting
welcome fires for Obon,

194
00:11:12,940 --> 00:11:15,200
but this old boozer needs
a hair of the dog instead.

195
00:11:16,940 --> 00:11:18,280
There's some here too.

196
00:11:18,820 --> 00:11:20,520
Sake lying right on the road, of all things!

197
00:11:22,400 --> 00:11:23,960
It's pure heaven.

198
00:11:27,360 --> 00:11:28,520
There's some over there too.

199
00:11:29,040 --> 00:11:31,060
What a shameless drinker.

200
00:11:31,640 --> 00:11:33,560
For a ghost, he's got legs too.

201
00:11:34,640 --> 00:11:35,400
Wobble, wobble.

202
00:11:35,400 --> 00:11:37,040
Is there no more sake?

203
00:11:37,040 --> 00:11:38,440
Look at the old man.

204
00:11:38,440 --> 00:11:40,660
You polished off a whole
bottle all by yourself.

205
00:11:40,660 --> 00:11:41,460
A whole bottle?

206
00:11:41,460 --> 00:11:45,860
There was a little left.

207
00:11:45,860 --> 00:11:47,560
What a terrifying drunk.

208
00:11:48,280 --> 00:11:49,200
Let me ask you one thing.

209
00:11:49,200 --> 00:11:51,240
Hey, old man, what's your name?

210
00:11:51,340 --> 00:11:53,600
Me? I'm Ryoma Sakamoto.

211
00:11:53,600 --> 00:11:54,160
What?

212
00:11:54,220 --> 00:11:55,327
Just kidding, just kidding.

213
00:11:55,377 --> 00:11:58,620
I'm Tameyoshi, that's my name.

214
00:11:58,620 --> 00:11:59,560
Just as I thought.

215
00:11:59,560 --> 00:12:01,940
Looks like you escaped from heaven.

216
00:12:01,940 --> 00:12:04,180
Hanayama's been searching for you,
looking frantic.

217
00:12:04,640 --> 00:12:06,640
Hanayama? Never heard of him.

218
00:12:06,640 --> 00:12:09,680
The old wizard, from the heaven police.

219
00:12:10,720 --> 00:12:13,260
Him? The one who got plastered in heaven?

220
00:12:13,260 --> 00:12:14,540
I might have looked after him a bit.

221
00:12:15,340 --> 00:12:17,500
You look like someone I've met somewhere.

222
00:12:18,280 --> 00:12:19,040
Who are you?

223
00:12:19,140 --> 00:12:20,880
I'm your son's -

224
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:21,760
Kanbi?

225
00:12:21,880 --> 00:12:22,980
His son's -

226
00:12:22,980 --> 00:12:23,660
Genji?

227
00:12:23,880 --> 00:12:26,260
Yes, and his son, Ryotsu Kankichi.

228
00:12:26,260 --> 00:12:27,540
You're my great-grandson.

229
00:12:27,540 --> 00:12:28,200
Kankichi?

230
00:12:28,300 --> 00:12:29,200
Don't know.

231
00:12:29,200 --> 00:12:30,560
Well, of course.

232
00:12:30,560 --> 00:12:32,640
I was born after you died, so.

233
00:12:32,640 --> 00:12:33,860
I see.

234
00:12:33,860 --> 00:12:36,080
Kankichi, you got no more sake?

235
00:12:36,340 --> 00:12:37,400
You're really something, you know.

236
00:12:37,400 --> 00:12:38,780
You drank it all in no time.

237
00:12:38,780 --> 00:12:39,700
There's none left.

238
00:12:39,700 --> 00:12:41,560
Even just half of this would do.

239
00:12:41,560 --> 00:12:42,620
Then I'll drink it.

240
00:12:43,000 --> 00:12:46,640
We'd better hand this old
man over to Hanayama soon.

241
00:12:46,640 --> 00:12:47,760
Ryo-san!

242
00:12:48,880 --> 00:12:52,960
Ryo-san, I'll go and fetch some valuable
photos from the Bakumatsu era right away.

243
00:12:53,380 --> 00:12:54,640
Valuable photos.

244
00:12:55,120 --> 00:12:59,200
It's not just photos. There's all sorts
of other stuff too. They're my treasures!

245
00:12:59,200 --> 00:13:01,820
Please, do show us those items.

246
00:13:01,820 --> 00:13:05,460
If you don't mind,
we'd like to buy them at a fair price.

247
00:13:05,900 --> 00:13:09,000
With the money from selling them,
I can drink sake.

248
00:13:09,000 --> 00:13:10,700
Sure, go ahead.

249
00:13:11,860 --> 00:13:12,240
Thank you very much.

250
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:15,400
Old man, you had such valuable things?

251
00:13:15,400 --> 00:13:17,700
Yes, they should be at my house in Asakusa.

252
00:13:18,160 --> 00:13:19,520
What, tsukudani?

253
00:13:19,520 --> 00:13:24,440
Before we send this old man back to heaven,
we can squeeze a drink out of him.

254
00:13:28,320 --> 00:13:29,880
Is it already Obon this year?

255
00:13:30,280 --> 00:13:33,340
That's right, if we dawdle,
it'll be autumn before we know it.

256
00:13:35,240 --> 00:13:39,940
Today I'm reporting on the exhibition on the late
Edo to early Meiji period being held in Ginza.

257
00:13:39,940 --> 00:13:42,260
Are you also a fan of Sakamoto Ryoma,
old man?

258
00:13:42,820 --> 00:13:45,240
No, I'm Tameyoshi Ryotsu.

259
00:13:45,420 --> 00:13:48,900
There, it's ready.
When Obon comes, our ancestors

260
00:13:48,950 --> 00:13:51,195
hurry back on horseback on the way here,

261
00:13:51,245 --> 00:13:53,540
and ride slowly back on an ox.

262
00:13:55,900 --> 00:13:59,284
Back in the day, we often brought tsukudani,
Ryoma-san's favorite,

263
00:13:59,334 --> 00:14:01,460
to the restaurant.

264
00:14:02,360 --> 00:14:03,480
Strange old man.

265
00:14:03,700 --> 00:14:04,440
N-no way.

266
00:14:04,540 --> 00:14:06,020
Hey, is there anyone here?

267
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:06,800
Oh my.

268
00:14:08,660 --> 00:14:10,900
You haven't changed a
bit since the old days.

269
00:14:12,260 --> 00:14:13,100
Is this a guest?

270
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:15,460
You're my wife, you know.

271
00:14:15,460 --> 00:14:18,360
So that means you're Genji's wife?

272
00:14:18,700 --> 00:14:20,460
That's right. Well, come on in.

273
00:14:20,460 --> 00:14:21,440
Please, please.

274
00:14:21,440 --> 00:14:25,140
Yeah, it's nice to come home
once in a while and settle down.

275
00:14:25,140 --> 00:14:27,720
That's right,
we both live in Tokyo, after all.

276
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:28,340
Tch, clack.

277
00:14:28,840 --> 00:14:30,080
Grandpa's on TV.

278
00:14:30,080 --> 00:14:30,660
Yo.

279
00:14:32,180 --> 00:14:33,380
Dad, what's wrong?

280
00:14:33,500 --> 00:14:35,420
T-the late old man Tameyoshi...

281
00:14:38,360 --> 00:14:40,260
What is this? That's outrageous!

282
00:14:40,260 --> 00:14:41,520
Isn't it beer?

283
00:14:42,260 --> 00:14:50,420
You've already had plenty, and you still want more sake?
Don't say that. Beer's no different from water.
No doubt about it, it's old Tameyoshi.

284
00:14:50,420 --> 00:14:57,280
What on earth is going on, Kankichi? Stop fussing.
It's Obon, so your ancestor has come back, hasn't he?

285
00:14:57,280 --> 00:15:07,260
Ah, I see. That's right. Your ancestor has come back after a long time, just now.
Yes, here you go.

286
00:15:09,540 --> 00:15:12,320
Looks like the tsukudani
still tastes the same.

287
00:15:13,500 --> 00:15:15,420
Grandpa, is the sake good?

288
00:15:15,420 --> 00:15:17,640
Delicious, delicious, delicious!

289
00:15:18,880 --> 00:15:19,580
I see.

290
00:15:20,920 --> 00:15:21,900
That's good.

291
00:15:22,720 --> 00:15:23,440
What is it?

292
00:15:23,440 --> 00:15:25,380
There was nothing in the garden shed.

293
00:15:25,380 --> 00:15:26,780
What are you talking about?

294
00:15:26,780 --> 00:15:29,820
Hey, old man!
He who doesn't work, doesn't eat.

295
00:15:29,820 --> 00:15:31,560
Help me search a little.

296
00:15:32,100 --> 00:15:33,980
Chief Ohara will be here soon, you know.

297
00:15:34,420 --> 00:15:35,660
Search for what?

298
00:15:37,260 --> 00:15:37,900
Treasure?

299
00:15:46,100 --> 00:15:49,380
Hey! That's it!

300
00:15:49,500 --> 00:15:50,560
What? Really?

301
00:15:50,860 --> 00:15:51,620
Excuse me for intruding.

302
00:15:51,620 --> 00:15:52,580
They're here!

303
00:15:54,100 --> 00:15:55,440
Then, let me take a look.

304
00:15:58,740 --> 00:16:01,120
It's a photo, and it must be really old.

305
00:16:03,320 --> 00:16:04,280
Ochoko?

306
00:16:04,540 --> 00:16:06,240
Phew, how nostalgic.

307
00:16:07,340 --> 00:16:08,180
T-this is...

308
00:16:08,180 --> 00:16:09,400
Bamboo leaf?

309
00:16:12,680 --> 00:16:15,500
These all seem pretty worthless, don't they?

310
00:16:15,500 --> 00:16:17,100
What about this photo?

311
00:16:17,180 --> 00:16:19,660
Yeah, it's a photo Ryoma took.

312
00:16:20,380 --> 00:16:22,560
And who's the person in this photo?

313
00:16:22,860 --> 00:16:24,360
Yes, that's me.

314
00:16:24,360 --> 00:16:26,080
I-I see.

315
00:16:26,080 --> 00:16:30,580
Don't you have any photos of Ryoma Sakamoto himself,
old man?

316
00:16:31,300 --> 00:16:32,740
Well, no, I don't.

317
00:16:32,740 --> 00:16:33,260
Yeah.

318
00:16:33,260 --> 00:16:35,540
You don't have any?
What a troublemaker you are.

319
00:16:37,260 --> 00:16:38,840
Then let's see some of the other things,
shall we?

320
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:44,140
Ryo-san... that one

321
00:16:44,610 --> 00:16:50,960
That's Natsume Soseki's cat.
You doted on this furball.

322
00:16:50,960 --> 00:16:57,980
Don't you have anything of his own?
This thing just looks like scrap paper.

323
00:16:57,980 --> 00:17:04,320
That's Higuchi Ichiyo's... Higuchi Ichiyo, the one who wrote
"Takekurabe"?

324
00:17:04,320 --> 00:17:06,918
You're well-informed, Mom. Then -

325
00:17:06,968 --> 00:17:09,440
Is that Ichiyo-san's manuscript?

326
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:13,779
No, it doesn't seem to be.

327
00:17:13,829 --> 00:17:15,100
What on earth is this...?

328
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:17,540
Washi paper Higuchi Ichiyo
used to wipe her brush.

329
00:17:17,840 --> 00:17:18,240
And this?

330
00:17:19,520 --> 00:17:22,940
Bamboo leaves cut by Chiba Shusaku,
the greatest swordsman under heaven.

331
00:17:23,340 --> 00:17:23,740
And this?

332
00:17:24,120 --> 00:17:26,440
The sake cup Ryoma-san drank from.

333
00:17:29,160 --> 00:17:31,360
Well, I'll be going now.

334
00:17:32,320 --> 00:17:33,200
Wait.

335
00:17:34,640 --> 00:17:37,520
Wait a second, if I search more,
there might be treasure

336
00:17:38,320 --> 00:17:41,900
since there are quite a lot of
things from that era in circulation,

337
00:17:41,900 --> 00:17:44,860
so even antiques dealers
just being old isn't enough to

338
00:17:44,860 --> 00:17:48,700
If real treasure turns up,
please contact us anytime.

339
00:17:49,220 --> 00:17:49,660
Well then.

340
00:17:51,200 --> 00:17:52,820
Sorry we had nothing to offer you.

341
00:17:52,820 --> 00:17:54,860
Thank you for your trouble.

342
00:17:54,860 --> 00:17:55,535
Damn it,

343
00:17:55,585 --> 00:18:00,120
and there's an old man who's practically
a certified living national treasure!

344
00:18:01,420 --> 00:18:02,960
Where'd he go? The bathroom?

345
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:04,980
Honestly,
there's no decent stuff here at all.

346
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:06,120
Yeah, you're right.

347
00:18:06,120 --> 00:18:09,280
Hey, I think the old man
went out the back door.

348
00:18:09,280 --> 00:18:10,020
What?

349
00:18:11,280 --> 00:18:14,320
That's strange, I'm sure it was around here.

350
00:18:17,600 --> 00:18:19,520
What's this, all of a sudden? Found him!

351
00:18:19,520 --> 00:18:20,840
Old man!

352
00:18:20,840 --> 00:18:21,800
Oi, Kankichi.

353
00:18:23,360 --> 00:18:26,540
Old man, if you vanish without a word,
people worry, you know.

354
00:18:26,540 --> 00:18:28,080
Shinanoya's gone.

355
00:18:28,080 --> 00:18:31,860
I always used to come here and get a drink on credit,
you know.

356
00:18:31,860 --> 00:18:32,860
Shinanoya?

357
00:18:33,300 --> 00:18:34,640
This is a convenience store, you know.

358
00:18:35,060 --> 00:18:37,160
Ryo-san, are you back home for a visit?

359
00:18:37,600 --> 00:18:38,600
I see.

360
00:18:38,600 --> 00:18:40,080
This used to be a liquor store.

361
00:18:40,080 --> 00:18:44,060
Yeah, selling only liquor
doesn't pay these days.

362
00:18:44,060 --> 00:18:47,080
Was the name of the liquor
store back then Shinanoya?

363
00:18:47,240 --> 00:18:49,840
No, ours was Mikawaya.

364
00:18:49,840 --> 00:18:50,960
Wait a minute.

365
00:18:51,380 --> 00:18:53,920
The drinking place my
grandfather ran before the war

366
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:56,000
was definitely Shinanoya.

367
00:18:56,540 --> 00:18:57,800
So it really was that place.

368
00:18:57,800 --> 00:18:59,980
So your classmate Yasu's shop was

369
00:18:59,980 --> 00:19:02,080
on the street along Seiko.

370
00:19:02,080 --> 00:19:02,860
Y-yeah.

371
00:19:02,860 --> 00:19:04,700
Then what about Okiku-san?

372
00:19:04,700 --> 00:19:05,780
She was up ahead, right?

373
00:19:05,780 --> 00:19:07,320
The round-faced beauty's

374
00:19:07,320 --> 00:19:07,900
Y-yeah.

375
00:19:08,760 --> 00:19:10,140
We've got a customer.

376
00:19:10,140 --> 00:19:11,700
Well then, Ryo-san, see you again.

377
00:19:13,280 --> 00:19:14,400
Okiku-san.

378
00:19:14,400 --> 00:19:15,080
Old man.

379
00:19:15,080 --> 00:19:17,380
That was over 100 years ago.

380
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:19,380
Nobody from back then is still alive.

381
00:19:20,280 --> 00:19:21,340
This is boring.

382
00:19:21,340 --> 00:19:23,080
I don't know anyone here.

383
00:19:23,080 --> 00:19:24,600
This isn't any fun.

384
00:19:26,540 --> 00:19:31,120
Isn't it? Well done, you found it!

385
00:19:31,490 --> 00:19:36,520
Let's take you back to heaven right away, come on!
No, no, I want more sake to drink!

386
00:19:36,520 --> 00:19:41,700
I don't want to go back yet.
Wait, our old man is here!

387
00:19:41,700 --> 00:19:46,920
Since you're doing this, you'll be
punished when you get back to heaven.

388
00:19:46,920 --> 00:19:49,860
Hey! What are you doing?

389
00:19:50,340 --> 00:19:53,360
Before I take the old man back,
I have one favor to ask.

390
00:19:53,360 --> 00:19:55,900
If it's about wiping
out your demerit points,

391
00:19:55,900 --> 00:19:58,920
forget that. It's a different favor.

392
00:20:00,940 --> 00:20:02,260
Then, do it for me.

393
00:20:02,700 --> 00:20:04,320
Only fifteen minutes, mind you.

394
00:20:04,800 --> 00:20:06,640
Well then, hoda hoda hoy!

395
00:20:06,640 --> 00:20:07,240
Yeah, yeah.

396
00:20:12,520 --> 00:20:13,860
Ryoma-san!

397
00:20:14,340 --> 00:20:16,060
What, Sakamoto Ryoma?

398
00:20:16,320 --> 00:20:18,320
Ryoma-san, and you?

399
00:20:18,500 --> 00:20:21,122
It's me. I've gotten old, but

400
00:20:21,172 --> 00:20:22,700
I'm Tameyoshi Ryotsu.

401
00:20:23,360 --> 00:20:32,180
Tameyoshi? So you really did die!
Chief, it's a disaster!
What's with the panic? The real ones are over there.

402
00:20:32,180 --> 00:20:38,600
Aaaah! Katsu Kaishu... and Saigo Takamori!

403
00:20:38,600 --> 00:20:47,520
Over there is Ito Hirobumi, and in front of him is Ii Naosuke.
Even Perry and Harris, Natsume Soseki, Higuchi Ichiyo, and Ishikawa Takuboku...

404
00:20:48,480 --> 00:20:50,480
The one who just came out was Mori Ogai.

405
00:20:50,480 --> 00:20:52,540
The woman behind him was Yosano Akiko.

406
00:20:52,540 --> 00:20:54,480
It's like I'm dreaming.

407
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:55,960
It's not a dream.

408
00:20:55,960 --> 00:20:58,000
Ryo-san.

409
00:20:58,000 --> 00:20:59,020
How about it?

410
00:20:59,020 --> 00:21:01,260
They're truly treasures, aren't they?

411
00:21:01,260 --> 00:21:03,780
The venue's packed with customers now.

412
00:21:03,780 --> 00:21:04,640
No way.

413
00:21:04,640 --> 00:21:08,200
Yeah, I have a few acquaintances in heaven.

414
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:09,120
Heaven.

415
00:21:09,560 --> 00:21:11,420
Numbered tickets are available at the front.

416
00:21:11,420 --> 00:21:12,720
Please wait a moment.

417
00:21:13,840 --> 00:21:14,600
Don't push.

418
00:21:16,860 --> 00:21:18,540
Yasu, I've missed you.

419
00:21:18,540 --> 00:21:19,860
Hey, pull yourself together.

420
00:21:19,860 --> 00:21:20,900
Tameyoshi-san.

421
00:21:21,540 --> 00:21:22,700
Grandpa.

422
00:21:22,700 --> 00:21:24,300
Old man, that's great.

423
00:21:24,300 --> 00:21:26,020
It's a present from me.

424
00:21:26,440 --> 00:21:29,620
Ee ja nai ka, ee ja nai ka, ee ja nai ka!

425
00:21:29,620 --> 00:21:31,000
Ee ja nai ka, yeah!

426
00:21:31,000 --> 00:21:31,940
They've all come out.

427
00:21:31,940 --> 00:21:33,100
What are these guys?

428
00:21:33,100 --> 00:21:35,660
By mistake, it went wildly viral.

429
00:21:35,660 --> 00:21:38,420
Even the Ee ja nai ka crowd has come out.

430
00:21:38,420 --> 00:21:38,960
What?

431
00:21:53,140 --> 00:21:54,520
Aaaaaaa

432
00:21:54,520 --> 00:21:54,780
Aaaaaaa

433
00:21:54,780 --> 00:21:55,740
Aaaaaaa

434
00:21:56,440 --> 00:21:59,920
Ee ja nai ka, ee ja nai ka, ee ja nai ka!

435
00:22:00,570 --> 00:22:05,320
Ee ja nai ka, ee ja nai ka, ee ja nai ka!

436
00:22:05,320 --> 00:22:09,080
Ee ja nai ka, ee ja nai ka, ee ja nai ka!

437
00:22:09,080 --> 00:22:10,660
Ee ja nai ka, ee ja nai ka, ee ja nai ka!

438
00:22:10,660 --> 00:22:12,120
So this is what Japan has become...

439
00:22:12,120 --> 00:22:13,960
Well, it's quite something indeed.

440
00:22:14,380 --> 00:22:16,720
Maybe opening the country
was a mistake after all.

441
00:22:16,720 --> 00:22:18,900
No, it was the perfect decision!

442
00:22:21,940 --> 00:22:25,020
That's it,
I'm sending everyone back to heaven!

443
00:22:25,020 --> 00:22:26,000
Wait!

444
00:22:26,780 --> 00:22:27,740
Just thirty seconds.

445
00:22:27,740 --> 00:22:29,820
Let me say goodbye to the old man.

446
00:22:30,960 --> 00:22:32,760
Fine, but hurry up.

447
00:22:32,760 --> 00:22:34,280
Thanks!

448
00:22:35,100 --> 00:22:37,280
Old man, it's almost time to say goodbye.

449
00:22:37,280 --> 00:22:38,900
Is it already time?

450
00:22:38,900 --> 00:22:41,900
Old man, thanks to you, I had a fun Obon.

451
00:22:42,120 --> 00:22:43,900
Make sure you watch over
us next year's Obon too.

452
00:22:44,280 --> 00:22:46,320
I'll prepare plenty of sake for you.

453
00:22:46,980 --> 00:22:49,620
Time's up for the ceremony at the base.

454
00:22:50,420 --> 00:22:59,820
Later, old man!

455
00:23:04,440 --> 00:23:06,460
who lived through the
late Edo and Meiji eras

456
00:23:06,460 --> 00:23:08,860
lookalikes of great historical
figures have all gathered!

457
00:23:08,860 --> 00:23:12,320
an unseasonal festival frenzy has
the main street in a panic, I hear.

458
00:23:12,960 --> 00:23:14,660
What, no appearance fee?

459
00:23:15,260 --> 00:23:16,860
That's not what we agreed on!

460
00:23:16,860 --> 00:23:18,060
Agreed?

461
00:23:18,340 --> 00:23:20,760
We're in a complete uproar here,
repairing the venue.

462
00:23:21,320 --> 00:23:24,020
We're the ones who should be
getting repair costs from you.

463
00:23:24,020 --> 00:23:27,700
Yesterday they got to meet the real Katsu Kaishu and Ryoma Sakamoto,
they said.

464
00:23:27,700 --> 00:23:29,880
But they were so happy about it!

465
00:23:29,880 --> 00:23:31,820
They can't possibly be the real thing.

466
00:23:32,960 --> 00:23:35,180
That's why scholars are
so stubborn and useless.

467
00:23:35,180 --> 00:23:35,940
Damn it!

468
00:23:36,920 --> 00:23:40,020
Senpai, you're not involved
in this commotion, are you?

469
00:23:40,020 --> 00:23:41,760
Yes, that's right, Ryo-chan.

470
00:23:41,760 --> 00:23:44,900
No, no,
I have nothing to do with it at all, Nosuke.

471
00:23:47,220 --> 00:23:49,000
"Nothing to do with it, Nosuke,"

472
00:23:51,140 --> 00:23:54,020
Looks like you've picked up my pet phrase.

473
00:23:54,760 --> 00:23:55,900
Exactly, man.

474
00:23:57,060 --> 00:23:58,560
I came back again.

475
00:23:59,900 --> 00:24:02,540
Didn't I tell you it's next year's Obon?

476
00:24:05,940 --> 00:24:09,060
Welcome! Yes, welcome!

477
00:24:09,820 --> 00:24:14,040
Yes, welcome, please come in! Yes, welcome!

478
00:24:14,620 --> 00:24:18,820
Yes, welcome, please come in! Yes, welcome!

479
00:24:19,340 --> 00:24:23,820
Welcome! Um, and and then, well...

480
00:24:23,820 --> 00:24:26,140
Excuse me, is it all right? Welcome!

481
00:24:26,140 --> 00:24:28,440
Then, a natto roll,
a salmon roll, a salad roll.

482
00:24:28,440 --> 00:24:30,280
Any kind of roll, rolls... what should I do?

483
00:24:30,960 --> 00:24:34,240
Right, how about a California roll?

484
00:24:37,020 --> 00:24:39,000
This isn't America, you know.

485
00:24:39,000 --> 00:24:40,520
Sorry, Sori.

486
00:24:40,520 --> 00:24:44,500
Uh, excuse me.

487
00:24:45,300 --> 00:24:46,280
Welcome!

488
00:24:47,240 --> 00:24:49,840
Then, kushiage, kakiage, katsuage.

489
00:24:49,840 --> 00:24:51,680
Anything fried, fried... what was it again?

490
00:24:52,160 --> 00:24:53,680
What do you recommend?

491
00:24:54,740 --> 00:24:56,940
Just watch out for the katsuage.

492
00:24:56,940 --> 00:25:00,680
Is that a dad joke?

493
00:25:00,680 --> 00:25:02,440
Yes, sorry, Sori.

494
00:25:02,440 --> 00:25:04,740
I don't get it at all.

495
00:25:06,080 --> 00:25:27,340
Huh huh huh huh huh...

496
00:25:29,760 --> 00:25:32,060
Hot, hot, hot, hot!

497
00:25:32,420 --> 00:25:35,180
I was wondering why
our dorm alone is so hot,

498
00:25:35,180 --> 00:25:37,860
and it's the glare bouncing off the
Mirror Building right in front of us.

499
00:25:37,860 --> 00:25:40,780
Damn it,
we've got to do something about this heat

500
00:25:40,780 --> 00:25:43,740
or I'll be baked like a
dried fish before summer ends!

501
00:25:44,120 --> 00:25:47,400
Next time, blow that scorching heat away.
See you!

502
00:25:47,400 --> 00:25:50,740
Over there, Kame-ari!

503
00:25:52,020 --> 00:25:54,080
Well, surely there's Kame-ari!

504
00:25:55,340 --> 00:25:59,240
Everyone, come on over to our town!

